## 4. AUM / MEMORANDUM OF DUE LAYER

Materials expressly designated as **AUM**, **Memorandum of Due**, **AUM Document**, **ODS**, **ODS Retrieval**, **ORDINEXT**, **ORDINEXT-TERM**, **Sub**, or associated execution records remain subject to their own applicable Memorandum of Due and execution terms.

The AUM layer may include:

- AUM Document Code and document-specific identification;
- cryptographic document identification;
- ORDINEXT and ORDINEXT-TERM;
- ODS and ODS Retrieval;
- enumeration and relevant simulation;
- subjective mutuality and eligible vacancy;
- applicable PUB / Pub Point designations;
- Courtesying, Ordinal Courtesy, Initial Courtesy and Evidential Courtesy;
- AI Courtesy and AI-undertaken document-quality provisions;
- witnessing and execution schedules; and
- separately executed delivery, remuneration, liability or other provisions.

**Separation rule:** An AUM term is not automatically incorporated into a CC BY-ND work, Apache-licensed work, psychiatric/therapeutic work, or third-party work merely because it is stored in the same repository.

## 5. PSYCHIATRIC / MEDICAL / THERAPEUTIC PRACTICE LAYER

Materials designated for **Psychiatric Administration**, **medical practice**, **therapeutic practice**, **Infirmation**, tariff construction, therapeutic registration, clinical/administrative documentation, or related practice records constitute a separate documentation layer.

Unless an individual file expressly carries another licence:

**No general open-source or open-content licence is granted merely by inclusion in this repository.**

Publication on GitHub or another public host does not, by itself, convert restricted practice documentation into Apache-licensed, CC-licensed, or public-domain material.

Nothing in this document constitutes a medical licence, governmental registration, clinical credential, or regulatory approval.

## 6. APACHE-COMPATIBLE SOFTWARE INSULATION

### 6.1 Apache-designated components

A source file, code directory, software component, or other material is governed by **Apache License 2.0** only where it is expressly designated as such, for example by:

- `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`;
- an Apache-2.0 source header;
- a component-level LICENSE notice; or
- an explicit component licence declaration.

Canonical Apache licence:
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

### 6.2 Insulation / non-conflation rule

Apache-2.0 terms apply **only to components designated Apache-2.0**.

They do not automatically:

- relicense CC BY-ND material;
- permit distribution of CC BY-ND Adapted Material;
- modify an executed AUM;
- grant rights in proprietary psychiatric/medical/therapeutic documentation;
- transfer patents or trademarks belonging to the Principal or third parties;
- convert restricted practice records into open-source software; or
- impose Apache-2.0 obligations upon material that is not Apache-2.0 licensed.

Conversely, CC BY-ND, AUM, psychiatric/therapeutic, or other proprietary terms do not automatically modify an Apache-2.0 component.

Apache's licensing guidance distinguishes Apache material from third-party works and addresses required licensing and NOTICE information. citeturn0search0turn0search1

## 7. MIXED-REPOSITORY RULE

A repository containing several licence layers is **not thereby a single uniformly licensed work**.

| Material | Governing layer |
|---|---|
| File expressly marked CC BY-ND 4.0 | CC BY-ND 4.0 |
| Executed Memorandum of Due / AUM record | Its executed AUM terms |
| Designated psychiatric/medical/therapeutic material | Its stated terms; otherwise reserved |
| File expressly marked Apache-2.0 | Apache License 2.0 |
| Third-party material | Its own stated licence |
| Unmarked original material | Rights reserved unless this notice expressly grants a licence |

Where a composite distribution contains separately licensed components, the licences remain **component-specific**.

## 8. NO IMPLIED RELICENSING

Nothing in this umbrella notice:

- relicenses a third-party work;
- alters a Creative Commons licence;
- creates an Apache-2.0 licence where none was designated;
- waives an AUM requirement;
- waives attribution;
- authorizes adaptation where the applicable licence prohibits distribution of adaptations;
- grants patent rights beyond those expressly granted by the applicable licence;
- grants trademark rights;
- grants publicity or personality rights; or
- creates agency, endorsement or affiliation with Creative Commons, Apache Software Foundation, Google, Binance, Meta, Linktree, or another third party.

